# Supabase enhancement boundary

**Binding:** [ADR-004: Account and cloud enhancement model](../adrs/ADR-004-account-and-cloud-enhancement-model.md) (Accepted), [ADR-006: Serverless and secret boundary](../adrs/ADR-006-serverless-and-secret-boundary.md) (Accepted). **Local system of record:** [ADR-002](../adrs/ADR-002-local-data-ownership.md). **Product baseline:** [ADR-001](../adrs/ADR-001-product-operating-model.md). **Sync semantics:** [ADR-005](../adrs/ADR-005-sync-and-conflict-resolution.md) (Accepted). **Schemas at boundaries:** [ADR-008](../adrs/ADR-008-schema-led-domain-contracts.md). **Self-hosting:** [ADR-011](../adrs/ADR-011-self-hosting-provider-model.md) (Accepted). **Layering:** [`src/lib/api/session/README.md`](../src/lib/api/session/README.md), [`src/lib/api/cloud/README.md`](../src/lib/api/cloud/README.md), [`src/lib/api/README.md`](../src/lib/api/README.md).

## What Supabase is allowed to own

- **Auth/session identity**, **account-scoped remote storage** for backup/sync/share, and **permission-backed capability checks** for those enhancements only.
- **Not** the anonymous recipe book runtime source of truth: Dexie remains primary on-device ([ADR-002](../adrs/ADR-002-local-data-ownership.md)); cloud rows are replicas/enhancements ([ADR-004](../adrs/ADR-004-account-and-cloud-enhancement-model.md), [ADR-005](../adrs/ADR-005-sync-and-conflict-resolution.md)).

## Wiring conventions

- **Session client factories:** Cookie-backed clients are created through [`src/lib/api/session/`](../src/lib/api/session/) — do not call `createClient` or `@supabase/ssr` constructors directly in routes, hooks, or domain services.
- **Anonymous cloud reads:** Server-only public paths use `createAnonymousCloudClient` from [`src/lib/api/cloud/cloud.client.ts`](../src/lib/api/cloud/cloud.client.ts).
- **Server request client:** `src/hooks.server.ts` attaches `event.locals.supabase` via `createRequestServerClient`, with validated session via `safeGetSession` (JWT checked with `getUser`, not session alone).
- **Universal layout client:** `src/routes/+layout.ts` builds `data.supabase` via `createLayoutBrowserClient` (browser) or `createLayoutServerClient` (SSR); trusted `session` / `user` data comes from `+layout.server.ts` via `locals.safeGetSession`.
- **Privileged credentials:** use **only** browser-safe project keys in client and SSR client graphs; **never** import service-role or other privileged Supabase secrets into client graphs or shared modules ([ADR-006](../adrs/ADR-006-serverless-and-secret-boundary.md)).
- **Remote recipe/cloud mutations:** prefer `CloudService` / `SyncService` under `src/lib/api/cloud/` (constructor-injected `SupabaseClient` + `userId`) rather than scattering ad hoc table access ([ADR-004](../adrs/ADR-004-account-and-cloud-enhancement-model.md) enforcement). **`$lib/api/common`** holds cross-domain schemas/types only — see [`src/lib/api/common/README.md`](../src/lib/api/common/README.md).
- **Auth and session code:** Supabase JWT validation and sign-in/out belong in **`$lib/api/auth/`** (`AuthService`). Session **transport** (cookie adapters, layout client wiring) belongs in **`$lib/api/session/`**. Do **not** add auth or permission logic under `$lib/utils/` — see [ADR-008 §8](../adrs/ADR-008-schema-led-domain-contracts.md) and [`src/lib/utils/README.md`](../src/lib/utils/README.md).

## Auth, sharing, and backup — client surfaces

**Authoritative wiring** for Supabase in the browser and on the server is the table below.

| Surface | Factory | Role | Typical files |
| ------- | ------- | ---- | ------------- |
| **`event.locals.supabase`** | `createRequestServerClient` | Per-request SSR client. Cookie-backed session; used by **`safeGetSession`**, auth **form actions** (`signInWithPassword`, `verifyOtp`, etc.), and the **`authGuard`** chain that sets `event.locals.session`, `user`, and `permissions`. | [`src/hooks.server.ts`](../src/hooks.server.ts), [`src/routes/auth/+page.server.ts`](../src/routes/auth/+page.server.ts), [`src/routes/auth/confirm/+server.ts`](../src/routes/auth/confirm/+server.ts) |
| **`data.supabase` from layout load** | `createLayoutBrowserClient` / `createLayoutServerClient` | Universal client for session reads, **`CloudService` / `AccountService`**, and other layout consumers. Trusted SSR session/user values come from `+layout.server.ts`. | [`src/routes/+layout.ts`](../src/routes/+layout.ts), [`src/routes/+layout.server.ts`](../src/routes/+layout.server.ts) |
| **Anonymous server reads** | `createAnonymousCloudClient` | Server-only public cloud paths (e.g. share-by-token GET). **Not** for login or user-scoped cloud work. | [`src/routes/api/share/[token]/+server.ts`](../src/routes/api/share/%5Btoken%5D/+server.ts) |

**Backup, sync, and sharing** behavior and layering: [ADR-004](../adrs/ADR-004-account-and-cloud-enhancement-model.md), [`src/lib/api/cloud/README.md`](../src/lib/api/cloud/README.md). **Session factory reference:** [`src/lib/api/session/README.md`](../src/lib/api/session/README.md). **Secrets and which keys may appear in client graphs:** [ADR-006](../adrs/ADR-006-serverless-and-secret-boundary.md).

## New and changed Supabase-related work

- **Logged out / offline / missing permission:** core local recipe flows stay usable; cloud actions **degrade** (disable, defer, explain) instead of breaking unrelated UI ([ADR-004](../adrs/ADR-004-account-and-cloud-enhancement-model.md) continuity).
- **Validation:** treat Supabase responses like any external I/O—validate with Zod (or equivalent) before trusting shapes ([ADR-008](../adrs/ADR-008-schema-led-domain-contracts.md)).
- **Provider-agnostic discipline:** avoid encoding “WFD-managed Supabase only” into **domain contracts**, shared types, or permission logic that should later admit **user-hosted** databases with the same responsibilities ([ADR-004](../adrs/ADR-004-account-and-cloud-enhancement-model.md) self-hosting boundary; [ADR-011](../adrs/ADR-011-self-hosting-provider-model.md)).

